          "bodyExcerpt": "Wampler Pedals Pinnacle Deluxe v2 | Effects Database Skip to navigation Brands &#9660; 0-9... a... b... c... d... e... f... g... h... i... j... k... l... m... n... o... p... q... r... s... t... u... v... w... x... y... z... Effect types &#9660; boost distortion fuzz overdrive acoustic simulation amp simulation speaker/cabinet simulation chorus flanger phaser tremolo vibe vibrato other modulation pitch shifter octaver delay reverb looper/sampler hold/freeze eq filter wah fuzz-wah bitcrusher ring modulator samplerate reducer wavefolder synth effect granular effect multi effect vocal effect talkbox vocoder buffer compressor other... Countries &#9660; (country unknown) Argentina Australia Austria Belarus Belgium Brazil Bulgaria Canada Chile China Colombia Costa Rica Croatia Czech Republic Czechoslovakia DDR Denmark Dominican Republic Ecuador Egypt Estonia Finland France Germany Greece Hungary India Indonesia Iran Ireland Israel Italy Japan Latvia Lithuania Luxembourg Macedonia Malaysia Malta Mexico Moldova Monaco Morocco Netherlands New-Zealand Norway Panama Peru Philippines Poland Portugal Romania Russia Serbia Singapore Slovakia Slovenia South-Africa South-Korea Spain Sweden Switzerland Taiwan Thailand Turkey U.K. U.S.A. U.S.S.R. Ukraine Uruguay Venezuela Browse by &#9660; Enclosure type Modulation type Special &#9658; Classics Eye candy Funny Vaporware Weird Random brand Random effect Events &#9658; NAMM Musikmesse Music China Guitar Summit More... &#9660; Forum (opens in new tab) myFXDB (opens in new tab) Newsletter About How to get listed? Interviews Reviews Effects explained Books D.I.Y. Schematics Links Contact Install Effects Database App Search the database browse by brand I... IndyGuitarist Wampler Pedals browse by type volume/amplification amplification preamp / clean boost browse by type distortion/fuzz/overdrive distortion browse by enclosure pedal Wampler Pedals Pinnacle Deluxe v2 Published on November 3, 2016 Wampler Pedals boost / preamp distortion pedal Information The Wampler Pinnacle Deluxe v2 is a high-gain distortion pedal engineered to deliver the celebrated EVH-inspired \"Brown Sound\" while offering significantly expanded tonal control and flexibility over earlier versions. Originally introduced as the Pinnacle, the circuit was praised by Zeke Clark, longtime guitar technician for Eddie Van Halen, for authentically capturing the aggressive mids, harmonic saturation, and dynamic response associated with classic hot-rodded amplifier tones. Over time, the design evolved from a straightforward high-gain distortion with interactive tone shaping into a more versatile platform capable of covering everything from mild overdrive to modern high-gain rock and metal. The original Pinnacle featured four primary controls: Gain, Volume, and two interactive tone controls that functioned similarly to a parametric-style EQ, allowing users to sweep from scooped midrange textures to thick, warm mids. A Bright switch provided additional high-frequency emphasis for darker amplifiers, while a Gain Boost toggle altered the internal gain structure to shift the pedal from overdrive into more aggressive distortion territory. The Standard and Deluxe versions shared the same core tone, with the Deluxe model replacing the Gain Boost toggle with a dedicated footswitch for on-the-fly activation and adding an internal volume trim for extended output headroom. The Deluxe enclosure was correspondingly larger to accommodate the added switching. The Pinnacle Deluxe v2 builds upon this foundation with a comprehensive redesign aimed at increased tonal sculpting and performance control. The original tone stack was replaced with an active 3-band EQ featuring dedicated Bass, Mids, and Treble controls. This expanded EQ section enables precise tone-shaping, from tight low-end punch and scooped mids to forward, cutting lead tones. Additional bright and bass boost options further extend the frequency response, allowing players to dial in enhanced sparkle",
